    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6cf72a6b-7f5c-53ee-89c4-60c564528c1e",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the triangle spanned by $p=⟨-3,6,0⟩$ and $q=⟨4,3,-6⟩.$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\times q & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(6\\cdot (-6)-0\\cdot 3)i-((-3)\\cdot (-6)-0\\cdot 4)j+((-3)\\cdot 3-6\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =-36i-18j-33k \\\\  & =⟨-36,-18,-33⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,p\\times q\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-36)^{2}+(-18)^{2}+(-33)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1296+324+1089} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2709} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{301}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{301}}{2}.\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "4255caa3-50ba-54fa-82a8-74962672c0b3",
