      ":question/id": "ff6ee37a-5df7-5240-8139-6d8ab72c6503",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate the area of the triangle spanned by $r=⟨5,-5,-4⟩$ and $t=⟨2,1,-1⟩.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\times t & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 5 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-5)\\cdot (-1)-(-4)\\cdot 1)i-(5\\cdot (-1)-(-4)\\cdot 2)j+(5\\cdot 1-(-5)\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =9i-3j+15k \\\\  & =⟨9,-3,15⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,r\\times t\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{9}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{15}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81+9+225} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{315} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{35}}{2}.\n$$",
