      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-5)\\cdot (-5)-(-3)\\cdot 1)i-(4\\cdot (-5)-(-3)\\cdot (-1))j+(4\\cdot 1-(-5)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =28i+23j-k \\\\  & =⟨28,23,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{28}^{2}+{23}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{784+529+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1314} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{146}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{146}}{2}.\n$$",
