      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\times t & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(6\\cdot (-5)-1\\cdot 6)i-(4\\cdot (-5)-1\\cdot 2)j+(4\\cdot 6-6\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-36i+22j+12k \\\\  & =⟨-36,22,12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,r\\times t\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-36)^{2}+{22}^{2}+{12}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1296+484+144} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1924} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{481}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{481}}{2}=\\sqrt{481}.\n$$",
