      ":question/problem": "Calculate the area of the triangle spanned by $a=⟨-5,4,3⟩$ and $b=⟨1,-1,-4⟩.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4\\cdot (-4)-3\\cdot (-1))i-((-5)\\cdot (-4)-3\\cdot 1)j+((-5)\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =-13i-17j+k \\\\  & =⟨-13,-17,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-13)^{2}+(-17)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169+289+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{459} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{51}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{51}}{2}.\n$$",
